# `skills/` used to be ignored outright (2ae7b2b, M4b). That bare pattern matched
# `.claude/skills/` at any depth, so every skill this project relies on — including the
# two coding-rules skills that are force-loaded before any backend/frontend edit — was
# invisible to git. They are instructions the next change is written from, so they need
# to travel in the same diff as the code they describe; a rule that silently deletes a
# domain concept has to be able to fix the skill that still teaches it.
# The only other `skills` dir is inside backend/.venv, already covered by backend/.gitignore.
.claude/settings.local.json
